<title>UK: Shanks &amp; McEwan 1996/97 pre-tax 22.9 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Shanks &amp; McEwan 1996/97 pre-tax 22.9 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year to March 29, 1997 (million stg unless stated).</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		7.7		    vs   6.6</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.6		    vs   2.4</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 3.9		    vs   3.6</p>
<p> Pretax		    22.9		    vs  19.5</p>
<p> Turnover		 144			vs 114</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the cull of cattle resulting from the Bovine Spongiform Encephalopathy scare yielded a three-year contract for the safe disposal of rendered meat and bone. The company said that this contract, together with greater electricity generation capacity within its waste services unit and the group's 'proven ability to generate cash,' provided a platform for further growth. Full company name - Shanks &amp; McEwan Group Plc</p>
<p>	  -- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
